# Runtime data served by AnnZarro — NOT committed.
#
# AnnZarro discovers datasets by scanning a directory at runtime: point the
# server's `data_dir` config at this `served-data/` directory (or symlink it
# into the instance data dir), drop one `.zarr` store per dataset under
# `datasets/`, and the `/api/<v>/datasets` endpoint lists them automatically
# (annzarro/server/routes/data_routes.py:list_all_datasets — directory scan,
# no hardcoded dataset list). Per-user sessions land under `sessions/`.
#
# These are large, host-specific runtime artifacts, so they stay out of git.
# Deployment-specific dataset content (which studies are served, how they were
# harmonized) is owned by the deployment, not by AnnZarro core.
datasets/
sessions/
